@startuml 06-submission-target-state
' =====================================================================
' submission_target lifecycle
' Traces to: FR-18, FR-29, FR-30, NFR-6
'
' One row per (submission, registered target). The states below are
' DERIVED from two columns, not stored in a status enum:
'
'   ai_needed     does this target want AI feedback
'   completed_at  when the AI phase finished with this row, NULL if it
'                 has not run yet. Set on success AND on failure.
'   last_error    set only if that finish was a failure
'
' Both grading modes behave identically here. IMMEDIATE and NIGHTLY
' differ only in WHEN the AI phase runs.
' =====================================================================

title submission_target -- derived states

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica

state "Wants feedback" as WANTS
state "Opted out" as OPTED
state "Feedback produced" as DONE
state "Attempted and failed" as FAILED

[*] --> WANTS : the submission first reports in.\nOne row per registered target,\nai_needed = TRUE

WANTS : ai_needed TRUE, completed_at NULL.
WANTS : In NIGHTLY mode this is exactly what the
WANTS : trigger queries. In IMMEDIATE it lasts
WANTS : only until the AI phase runs, moments
WANTS : later in the same container.

OPTED : ai_needed FALSE.
OPTED : Her suite called ai_not_needed, usually
OPTED : because the test passed. No tokens spent.

DONE : completed_at set, last_error NULL.
DONE : Feedback rows exist and have been spliced
DONE : into results.json.

FAILED : completed_at set, last_error recorded.
FAILED : The AI phase retried inside the run and
FAILED : still failed, so it appended a note to
FAILED : results.json saying feedback could not
FAILED : be generated.

WANTS --> OPTED : her suite calls\nai_not_needed(target)\nduring functional testing
WANTS --> DONE : AI phase produced feedback
WANTS --> FAILED : AI phase failed after\nits in-run retries

DONE --> [*]
OPTED --> [*]
FAILED --> [*]

note right of FAILED #FFF8DC
  **Failure is terminal, in both modes.**
  There is no cross-night retry and no attempt
  counter. Retries happen inside one AI phase
  run, with backoff on transient errors and none
  on deterministic ones, and never outlive the
  process.

  This is why completed_at is set here too.
  Leaving it NULL would mean the NIGHTLY trigger
  picked the row up again every night forever,
  since its query is exactly "ai_needed and
  completed_at IS NULL".

  What DOES get retried the next night is work
  that was never attempted, because the trigger
  job failed or a service was down. Those rows
  still have completed_at NULL. "The job did not
  run" self-heals; "grading ran and failed" does
  not.
end note

note as N2 #FFF8DC
  **Two questions, two mechanisms**
  ai_needed asks whether this target wants
  feedback. It is the token saving, and the
  instructor controls it from her own test suite.

  submission.ai_graded_submitted_at asks whether
  this submission is finished. The nightly
  trigger filters on it, so a graded submission
  is never rerun, and the AI phase re-checks it
  to catch reruns the trigger did not cause.
  (AD-9)

  Set that guard once every ai_needed row has
  completed_at set, whether it succeeded or
  failed.
end note

@enduml
